    contentEn: [
      "Let us start with the short answer: PageSpeed Insights is not a toy score checker. It is a decision surface that combines field data and laboratory diagnostics. Chrome documentation explains that PSI uses Lighthouse to audit a page and also integrates Chrome UX Report, or CrUX, to show how real users experience the page and origin.",
      "",
      "That distinction matters because many teams either relax when they see a green score or panic when they see yellow. The real commercial question is different: which issue is hurting real users, which issue is only a laboratory signal, and which improvement is important enough to affect SEO, conversion, or ad efficiency?",
      "",
      "In this guide, we explain how to read PageSpeed Insights properly, which interpretation mistakes waste the most time, and how technical and marketing teams can make better decisions from the same report. Pair it with our [Core Web Vitals optimization guide](/en/blog/core-web-vitals-optimizasyonu-rehberi-2026), our [Google Search Console performance report guide](/en/blog/google-search-console-performans-raporu-rehberi-2026), our [enterprise software services](/en/kurumsal-yazilim), and our [contact page](/en/iletisim).",
      "",
      "## What data does PageSpeed Insights actually show?",
      "",
      "Chrome's official documentation states that PSI combines two major inputs: CrUX field data and Lighthouse lab data. CrUX is aggregated real-user experience data. Lighthouse is a controlled technical audit. Understanding that difference already makes the report more useful.",
      "",
      "On the field side, PSI surfaces Core Web Vitals and other important metrics. The official guide highlights LCP, INP, and CLS, then adds supporting measures such as FCP and TTFB. On the lab side, PSI provides diagnostic opportunities and technical findings for the tested page state.",
      "",
      "### CrUX and Lighthouse do not have to say the same thing",
      "",
      "This is one of the most important practical lessons. A page can look good in Lighthouse while real-user experience is still weak. The reverse is also possible. Device quality, network conditions, third-party scripts, and traffic mix can change field data significantly.",
      "",
      "## Common interpretation mistakes",
      "",
      "### Treating one page score as the truth for the whole site",
      "",
      "PSI gives you insight on a URL, not a full information architecture. Homepages, blog posts, category pages, and product pages often fail for different reasons.",
      "",
      "### Looking only at the score and ignoring the audit narrative",
      "",
      "The official Lighthouse overview makes clear that Lighthouse is an automated quality-improvement tool and that failed audits explain both why the issue matters and how to improve it. The score is only the entry point.",
      "",
      "### Assuming every performance issue has the same SEO or business impact",
      "",
      "Not every technical flaw deserves the same urgency. Some issues directly affect user experience and crawl efficiency. Others are smaller refinements. Without prioritization, teams stay busy while commercial impact remains limited.",
      "",
      "## How should you read a PSI report more correctly?",
      "",
      "### Start with field data",
      "",
      "If real-user experience is weak, you have a real problem even if lab output looks acceptable. The first question should be whether CrUX shows trouble in LCP, INP, or CLS.",
      "",
      "### Use lab diagnostics to investigate causes",
      "",
      "Lighthouse then helps you form a technical hypothesis. Heavy JavaScript, oversized images, slow server response, too many redirects, or render-blocking resources often become visible here.",
      "",
      "### Look for patterns by page type",
      "",
      "Is the issue isolated to one article, or repeated across all product pages? Pattern detection matters more than one-off cleanup. In some cases, this becomes a broader frontend or platform problem that requires [enterprise software support](/en/kurumsal-yazilim).",
      "",
      "### Interpret performance inside SEO and conversion context",
      "",
      "Performance is not only about search engines. It also shapes whether users stay, read, tap, or submit. That is why PSI findings become more useful when paired with our [landing page optimization guide](/en/blog/landing-page-optimizasyonu-rehberi-2026) and our [GA4 and GTM conversion tracking guide](/en/blog/ga4-ve-gtm-ile-donusum-takibi-rehberi-2026).",
      "",
      "## Which metrics deserve more attention?",
      "",
      "### LCP",
      "",
      "This measures how quickly the largest visible piece of content appears. Hero sections, key product media, and large content blocks often influence it heavily.",
      "",
      "### INP",
      "",
      "This reflects how responsive the page feels after user interaction. It matters more when forms, menus, filters, and action-heavy UI are central to conversion.",
      "",
      "### CLS",
      "",
      "This captures unexpected layout movement. Popups, late-loading media sizes, and unstable ad slots often create trust and usability problems here.",
      "",
      "### FCP and TTFB",
      "",
      "These complete the story by showing how early the page first paints and how fast the server responds with initial bytes.",
      "",
      "## Who should care most about PageSpeed Insights?",
      "",
      "Sites that expect leads or sales from SEO, paid landing pages, e-commerce catalogs, and corporate sites carrying accumulated technical debt should care a lot. If the business problem is 'we get traffic but the page does not convert well enough', PSI is not just a technical report. It is a commercial prioritization tool.",
      "",
      "It also matters for smaller businesses because it helps them avoid wasting budget on random fixes. Instead of rebuilding everything, they can identify the issue patterns that matter most first.",
      "",
      "## How does Celebix use this data?",
      "",
      "At Celebix, we do not stop at the score. We read field data and lab diagnostics separately, then map them against page type, business intent, and conversion path. We prefer to start on pages where technical improvement is most likely to affect revenue or lead quality.",
      "",
      "The goal is not to clear every audit line item. The goal is to reduce the actual friction that users and search engines feel. If you want clearer technical SEO and performance priorities, you can review our [digital marketing services](/en/dijital-pazarlama) or reach out through our [contact page](/en/iletisim).",
      "",
      "## Frequently Asked Questions",
      "",
      "### Are PageSpeed Insights and Lighthouse the same thing?",
      "",
      "No. PSI includes Lighthouse diagnostics, but it also combines them with CrUX field data from real-user experience.",
      "",
      "### Is a yellow score automatically bad for SEO?",
      "",
      "No. You need to examine which metric is affected, on which page type, and whether real users are actually experiencing the problem.",
      "",
      "### Should I look at field data or lab data first?",
      "",
      "Usually field data first. If real users show a problem, lab data becomes the place to diagnose likely causes.",
      "",
      "### Does every performance problem require code changes immediately?",
      "",
      "No. Sometimes image handling, third-party script governance, cache behavior, or page structure will matter more than a large code rewrite.",
      "",
      "## Conclusion: PageSpeed Insights is a decision tool, not a vanity score",
      "",
      "When you read PageSpeed Insights correctly, technical SEO and performance work become more defensible. When you read it badly, teams chase scores while the real user problem stays in place. Celebix can help translate PSI output into a clearer improvement roadmap tied to business goals."
    ],
