    contentEn: [
      "One of the rising concepts in Google Trends has been 'AI Overviews'. The reason is simple: users are no longer moving only through blue links. On some searches, they now expect faster summaries, comparisons, and context near the top of the experience. That naturally creates a new question for content teams: how is SEO changing?",
      "",
      "The short answer is that SEO is not ending, but shallow content is losing value faster. In an AI-assisted search experience, content that simply repeats keywords becomes weaker than content that clearly matches intent, earns trust, and provides meaningful structure.",
      "",
      "In this guide, we explain how SEO strategy should be read in the AI Overviews era, which content structures matter more, and how internal linking should support commercial pages. For content planning foundations, our [Google Trends content-planning guide](/en/blog/google-trends-ile-icerik-planlama-2026) is a useful companion.",
      "",
      "## Why are AI Overviews important for SEO?",
      "",
      "Because the attention economy on the search-results page is changing. In some queries, users can get a quick frame, a comparison, or a summarized answer before they explore deeper. That reduces the value of thin, repetitive content built only to capture traffic.",
      "",
      "At the same time, content with stronger expertise signals, clearer context, and a better next-step path becomes more useful. SEO is still about being found, but it is increasingly also about being trusted and chosen.",
      "",
      "## Which types of content may perform better?",
      "",
      "### Content that clearly matches search intent",
      "",
      "If a user searches for 'AI Overviews SEO', they rarely want a definition alone. They want impact, interpretation, and action. That means stronger content should combine explanation, implications, and practical next steps.",
      "",
      "### Content that adds an original framework",
      "",
      "Many articles repeat the same basic points. In the AI era, the difference often comes from giving the reader a better decision framework instead of simply rephrasing common information. For example, showing SMEs which content should be produced first is more useful than saying 'SEO matters.'",
      "",
      "### Content connected to commercial pages",
      "",
      "Informational articles are not enough on their own. They should naturally connect to service pages, offer pages, and conversion steps. That is why internal links to pages such as our [digital marketing services](/en/dijital-pazarlama) matter both for SEO and for conversion quality.",
      "",
      "## The most common SEO mistakes in the AI Overviews era",
      "",
      "### Publishing content that is too broad and too shallow",
      "",
      "Copying a topic headline and producing a generic explanation is now a weaker strategy. Readers can find similar sentences across hundreds of pages. Content that does not add a new decision-making frame struggles to stand out.",
      "",
      "### Leaving content disconnected from commercial intent",
      "",
      "Even if a blog post attracts traffic, it has limited business value if it does not lead the reader toward a relevant service, solution, or contact step. On business websites, blog content should support the decision journey rather than live in isolation.",
      "",
      "### Ignoring internal linking",
      "",
      "Topic clusters matter even more in the AI era. One article may define the main theme while others cover applied details, supporting angles, or local variations. A strong internal-linking structure helps both users and search engines understand topic depth.",
      "",
      "## How should content strategy be updated?",
      "",
      "### Build around topic clusters",
      "",
      "Instead of publishing isolated posts, it is usually more effective to create supporting clusters around a core commercial theme. For example, a Google Ads service page becomes stronger when supported by budget optimization, audit, invalid-click, and local consulting articles.",
      "",
      "### Define the next step in every piece",
      "",
      "Where should the reader go after finishing the article? To another guide, a service page, or a contact action? That answer should be built naturally into the content. Otherwise the article informs without helping the business outcome.",
      "",
      "### Add practical structure and firsthand framing",
      "",
      "A business site does not always need research-heavy documents, but it does need practical structure. Actionable frameworks such as grouping search intent first and then building internal-link layers make content more useful and more durable.",
      "",
      "### Let blog content strengthen service pages",
      "",
      "In the AI Overviews era, the connection between blog and service pages becomes even more important. Our [corporate website and SEO guide](/en/blog/kurumsal-web-sitesi-tasarim-seo-rehberi-2026) and [e-commerce SEO and conversion mistakes guide](/en/blog/e-ticaret-sitesi-kurarken-seo-ve-donusum-hatalari) are examples of how support content can reinforce core offers.",
      "",
      "It also matters to make the answer structure easier to scan. Clear H2-H3 flow, short summary paragraphs, question-based subheadings, and logical internal-link transitions help both users and search engines understand that the content is organized rather than improvised.",
      "",
      "## What does this shift mean for SMEs?",
      "",
      "For SMEs, the opportunity is not to compete with bigger sites on content volume alone. The opportunity is to build clearer, tighter, more commercially aligned topic clusters. Content that answers real questions, respects local context, and naturally connects to offer pages is more valuable than mass volume.",
      "",
      "That is why fewer but stronger articles often outperform a large library of shallow content. This difference is even clearer for local and service-based businesses.",
      "",
      "## How does Celebix look at this transition?",
      "",
      "At Celebix, we do not read AI Overviews only as a ranking threat. We see it as a chance to strengthen content quality, cluster logic, and the conversion journey. Every article is planned with search intent, internal linking, related service pages, and a next-step CTA in mind.",
      "",
      "The goal is not only to appear in search. It is to move the right user from the right topic to the right page. That makes content production more sustainable and commercially useful over time.",
      "",
      "If you want to update your content strategy for the AI Overviews era, strengthen your internal linking clusters, and support your service pages more effectively with SEO content, Celebix can help. You can reach us through our [contact page](/en/iletisim) for a deeper review.",
      "",
      "## FAQ",
      "",
      "### Do AI Overviews end SEO?",
      "",
      "No. But they do reduce the value of shallow, repetitive content. Clearer, more trustworthy, and better-structured content becomes more important.",
      "",
      "### Is publishing blog posts alone enough?",
      "",
      "No. Blog posts, service pages, and internal-link structure should work together.",
      "",
      "### Which content creates the biggest difference?",
      "",
      "Content that answers the real question, adds a useful framework, and leads to the next step becomes more valuable.",
      "",
      "### What is the most practical starting point for SMEs?",
      "",
      "Define the main commercial service clusters first, then plan supporting blog content around user intent.",
      "",
      "## Conclusion: in the AI era, the winning content is not just more content, but more meaningful content",
      "",
      "AI Overviews are making SEO more structural. It is no longer enough to mention the keyword. The content has to explain the topic, create context, and move the user toward the next step.",
      "",
      "Celebix can help build those clusters in a stronger, more commercial, and more sustainable way."
    ]
